  "source": "Centreline traced from OpenStreetMap (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) - see centrelineSource. The 18 named points are positions on that traced line, not hand-placed guesses: 'Start/Finish' is OSM node 1578189278 (the circuit's own start-finish node, which the line is rotated to start at), 'T1 Entry' is the braking reference ~120 m before T1 on the pit straight, 'Back Straight Mid' is the midpoint of Sepang's 927 m back straight between T14 and T15, and each apex is a local curvature maximum of the traced line. Turn numbering comes from matching those curvature maxima to the published character of each corner in lap order (clockwise): T4 is the 90-degree Langkawi right, T5/T6 the Genting esses, T7/T8 the KLIA double apex, T9 the Berjaya Tioman hairpin, T14 the 90-degree right onto the back straight and T15 the final hairpin. At a 20 m sample the T7/T8, T10/T11 and T13/T14 pairs each read as one continuous bend, so within those pairs the two apexes are the bend's two curvature peaks. Elevations are the previous close-but-not-surveyed estimates - same honesty standard as the strategy engine.",
